## 9. Tests (input → expected output)

**Single node, hand-built messages**
| Test | Input | Expected |
|------|-------|----------|
| Propose on follower | `Propose("x")` on a follower | returns false, log unchanged |
| Reject missing prev | follower with log length 2 gets `PrevLogIndex: 5` | `Reject: true`, log unchanged |
| Reject wrong prev term | follower has index 2 at term 1, message says `PrevLogTerm: 2` | `Reject: true` |
| Append | follower gets valid Prev + 2 entries | log grows by 2, reply `Index` = new last index |
| Conflict truncation | follower has `[1:t1, 2:t1, 3:t1]`, gets `Prev=(1,t1)`, entries `[2:t2]` | log becomes `[1:t1, 2:t2]` (old 2 and 3 deleted) |
| No truncation on match | follower has 1–3, gets an old message with `Prev=(0,0)`, entries `[1]` | log still has 1–3 |
| Commit learn | follower gets `LeaderCommit: 3` but message only covers up to 2 | `commitIndex = 2`, not 3 |

**Cluster, with the simulator.** Add a simulator helper that collects `CommittedEntries()` from every node after each tick, so you can compare them.
| Test | Input | Expected |
|------|-------|----------|
| Basic replication | 3 nodes, leader elected, `Propose("x")`, tick | every node applied `x` at the same index |
| Order | propose a, b, c | every node applies a, b, c in order, with no gaps or duplicates |
| Lagging follower | isolate a follower, propose 5, heal, tick | the follower catches up and applies all 5 |
| No majority, no commit | isolate the leader, `Propose` 3 entries to it, tick | those 3 never appear in anyone's committed entries |
| Overwrite uncommitted | continue: the others elect a new leader, commit 2 new entries; heal | the old leader's 3 entries are replaced; all logs identical |
| Figure 8 | set up logs by hand as in Figure 8 (c) | the leader does **not** commit the old-term entry by counting replicas |
| **Chaos** | 5 nodes, 200 seeds, 10% drops, random partitions, a proposal every few ticks to whoever is leader | Election Safety holds, **and** no two nodes ever apply different data at the same index |

**Done when:** all pass under `go test -race -count=20 ./raft/`, and you can explain without notes:
- why the consistency check guarantees whole-prefix matching
- why a leader can't commit an old-term entry by counting replicas
- why a follower must never truncate on a matching entry
- why `commitIndex` on a follower is capped at the last new entry

